# Byte-identity contract: the three deployed files must keep their exact bytes.
# index.html is LF text and is part of the published artifact, so force LF: git
# normalizes any CRLF away on commit, so a careless `git add` on Windows can
# never introduce CRLF and break the hash GitHub Pages serves. (An earlier
# `-text` rule stored the working copy verbatim, which let a stale CRLF working
# tree be committed as CRLF — the footgun this replaces.) The apk and favicon
# are genuinely binary.
index.html               text eol=lf
favicon.png              binary
litomysl-racing-game.apk binary

# Standard text files
*.md   text
*.yml  text
*.yaml text
*.json text
*.py   text
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Linguist / language stats:
# The deployed game is a 140 KB Pygbag Python+WebAssembly bundle, not HTML.
# Hide the wrapper HTML from the language bar; mark the apk bundle as vendored
# so Linguist doesn't pick a language for it either.
index.html               linguist-detectable=false
*.apk                    linguist-vendored
